WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much.
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I am 6'1."

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've been this height
since I was 12.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
Yes.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
First day of high school,
I walked into this --

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.
The teacher's here."

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.247 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
The rude girl in the front
raises his hand, like,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.718 line:92%
"Miss, ain't you our teacher?"

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.153 line:92%
"Um, no, I'm your classmate.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think this is,
'21 Jump Street?'"

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:23.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
Elementary school was worse,
because I was chunky.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, and when you're a fat ki
growing up,

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got to go the extra mile
to make friends.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was doing stuff like
magic and taxes.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.373
I'd be on the playground like,
"Abracadabra, it's an audit.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's play."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did get bullied
every once in a while.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
One day I came home from schoo
traumatized.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm crying in the mirror like,
"This is it.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.187
I don't have any friends.
I'm going to run away."

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my knees looked up
at me like,

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Baby, we ain't running
nowhere."

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.959 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:02.996 line:92%
My guardian angel pops up,

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Chloe, you can't run away
Tomorrow is pizza day.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:10.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ye-e-es!"

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.237 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Thank you, pepperoni.
I'm staying."

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, come on, don't act
like pizza day

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
wasn't the best day
of elementary school.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.979 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:20.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah!

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.715 line:92%
That cement block of dough

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
those two little Basquiat
paint brushes of tomato paste,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
the cheese -- the cheese,
it never melted.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.291 line:92%
It just stared at you like

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're going to get cance
at 50. Um...

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.328 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.896 line:92%
This is not real cheese."

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think about my childhood
a lot 'cause I'm not an adult.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.868
Yeah. My parents have been
married for over 40 years.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mom was 19. My dad was 24
when they got married.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.040 line:92%
Meanwhile, I'm 38, single,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.810
and I like to take picture
the of ugly babies in public

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, yeah, come on,
you can't get mad at me

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.850
for having pictures of you
gremlin in my smartphone.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.120 line:92%
Oh, if you're not laughing

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.389
uh, I probably got your relative
in my phone right now.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.228
I used to be a very mature
adult, don't get me wrong.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before I was a comedian,
I was a journalist.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did investigative reportin
for over a decade.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.435 size:75% position:38%
And then I realized,
people don't read.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.269 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so I found
another dream.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, in the eyes
of my parents, you know,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.007 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's a competition.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.977
My younger brother's 15 year
younger, and he's killing it

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.745 line:92%
So now my parents look at me

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.681 line:92%
like I'm the first pancake

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.751 size:81% position:41%
Mm-hmm. Yeah, you ever
go to make pancakes,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.653 size:81% position:41% line:92%
it's been a long time.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
The batter's extra lumpy.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're looking like, "Hopefull
it'll work itself out."

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.628 size:84% position:42%
You pour it in the pan.
The pan is way too hot.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
It burns instantly.
It's not even round,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's oblong staring up
at you like,

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mom, Dad, what are we going t
do about this?"

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like,
"Um, we're going to put yo

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:53.873
at the bottom of the stack
and hopefully in 38 years,

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody will want this
messed-up pancake."

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience "ahh"s ]
Oh, yeah, okay, fine.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.412 size:78% position:39% line:92%
All hope is not lost.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, my brother,
he went to Yale University

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.417 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.386 line:92%
But he majored in photography.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.923 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
At Yale University.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:16.296
Listen, y'all, it's time to warm
this pancake up, okay?

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:16.863 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, yeah, my parents
are devastated.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
They called me up,
"Chloe, can you please

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
talk some sense into
your brother?"

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mom, Dad,
don't worry about it."

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.337 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I called him up at Yale.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.739 line:92%
"Hey, Chad, follow your dreams."

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.541 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not an adult.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, listen, just because
you have a life dream

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.680 size:84% position:42%
and it doesn't pan out,
doesn't mean you throw

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.514 size:78% position:39% line:92%
your whole life away.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought I had my life
figured out.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was in my early 20s
me and my girlfriends

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.452 line:92%
would get together for brunch.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'd sit around the table,
talk about our future.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.892
"I'm going to get married.
You're going to get married.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:46.826 line:92%
You're going to get married.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to have a baby.
You're going to have a baby.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.763 line:92%
You're going to have a baby.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to start
a fashion line.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're going to start
a fashion line.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're going to
start a fashion line."

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.837 line:92%
None of us knew how to settle.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.572 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But now I'm almost 40.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:03.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
The conversation is
much more realistic.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.979
"I'm going to get a roommate
You're going to get a roommate

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.915
You're going to get a roommate."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.150
"I'm going to get a cat.
You're going to get a cat.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're going to get a cat.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to go to therapy.
You're going to therapy."

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you, guys.
My name is Chloe.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:28.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.937 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
